        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">About Me</p>
          <h2>Questions first, then models.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Dr. Lydia Moreno is an associate professor of Computational Neuroscience at Riverbend University’s School of Biological Sciences. Her work sits at 
the intersection of machine learning, systems neuroscience, and bioinformatics, aiming to unravel how neural circuits encode and process complex sensory 
information.</p>
          <p>She received her Ph.D. in Computational Biology from Baywood Institute of Technology and completed postdoctoral training in high-throughput imaging
analysis at Northborough Research Center. Her research combines theory-driven modeling with open, reproducible computational pipelines.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

